/* Recorded laboratory experiments, for the Simulate tab's Literature mode (js/sim_lit.js plays them on the 3D bench,
   js/lab3d.js). Loaded as a plain script, so a double-clicked page can read it.

   WHERE EACH THING COMES FROM — the page shows these differently, and they must never be mixed:
     text, adds, time, temp, see, yieldNote, product   the published source (quantities, times, temperatures, yields,
                                   melting/boiling points and observations are the source's own; ranges stay ranges)
     derived                       arithmetic from the source's numbers, shown with the working
     why                           this app's explanation of the chemistry (not in the source)
     cue                           what the 3D drawing shows that the source does not state (a colour, the bubbling);
                                   an illustration, labelled as such
     contents, bench positions, colours   how the bench is drawn: liquid heights come from the stated volumes; colours
                                   are illustrative
   Sources are openly licensed wherever possible (Creative Commons licences that allow adaptation — CC BY, BY-SA, BY-NC,
   BY-NC-SA — never ND), and every source states its licence in source.licence. Organic Syntheses is NOT used: its terms of
   use forbid storing its content (checked 2026-09-29), and tools/test_lab_experiments.js fails if it is cited.
   Step wording is this app's own paraphrase; source.url links the procedure as published. Where a source gives no
   yield, the experiment says so (yield.kind 'none'); a stated expectation is not shown as a measured yield.

   Shape:
     { id, title, summary, technique[], variantOf?, source: {text, doi?, url, free, licence?, kind},
       yield: {kind: 'measured'|'expected'|'example'|'none', text},
       substances: { key: {name, smiles?, cas?, mw?, density?, role, note?} },
       bench: [ {id, kind, label, x, z, y?, volume?, on?, under?, around?, stand?, holds?, hidden?, ...} ],   (js/lab3d.js)
       steps: [ {title, text, vessel?, frame?: [ids] (the camera frames these together), adds?: [{key, g?, ml?, mol?, note?}], contents?: {vesselId: {label, color, items,
                  cloudy?, bubbling?, stirring?, dripping?, fuming?, solid?, layers?, ml?} | null}, heat?: {id: 0..1},
                  visible?: {id: bool}, reading?: {thermometerId | meltempId: °C}, readingNote?, flame?: {burnerId: colour},
                  pour?: {from, to}, time?, temp?, see?, cue?, why?, derived?, yieldNote?, safety?} ],
       contents may also carry solid: [{depth, color, label}, …] (a packed column, bottom first), coat: {color} (crystals
       on a culture dish's lid) and plate: {front, lanes, spots: [{lane, rf, color}]} (a TLC plate; spot heights are
       illustrations unless the source gives Rf values, and say so in cue).
       notes: [string], safety: [string] }
*/
