      notes: ['The source quotes the Merck Index: aspirin melts at 135 °C (rapid heating), and 1 g dissolves in 300 mL of water at 25 °C or in 100 mL at 37 °C — which is why the washes use cold water.',
        'The source warns that the reaction also forms a little polyester, from salicylic acid acting as both the acid and the alcohol.'],
      safety: ['Concentrated sulfuric and hydrochloric acids are highly corrosive; acetic anhydride is corrosive and a lachrymator.', 'Ethyl acetate and petroleum ether are flammable: steam bath, no flames.', 'Phenol is toxic and is absorbed through the skin.'],
